- sys/types
+  twig
  '  One slot-value pair: the unit a myth is built from.
  :  slot=path =pail
+  myth
  '  The record at a node: slots (paths, used as opaque keys) to
  '  pails.  The unit of state the namespace versions and a behavior
  '  manipulates.  A myth holds a handful of slots, so it is an
  '  ordered map (/mop), not a tree — and a type alias, so the whole
  '  mop method set (get/put/size/uni) applies directly.
  mop[path pail lt_pith]
  +  new
    '  The empty myth.
    ^  myth
    (mop/empty)
  +  sing
    '  The one-slot myth.
    \  slot=path v=pail
    ^  myth
    |  mop/sing[path pail lt_pith] slot v
  +  meld
    '  Union; the add side wins collisions (the default talk law).
    \  add=myth cur=myth
    ^  myth
    cur.uni(add)
  ' TODO: needs wet namespace-modules
  '  +  gett
  '    (@ v)
  '    \ slot=path mit=myth
  '    ^ maybe[v]
  '    mit.get(slot).map(v/try_from_pail)
  +  add
    '  Chain one twig onto a myth: mit.add(twig).
    \  =twig mit=myth
    ^  myth
    mit.put(twig.slot twig.pail)
+  lock
  '  One care's two independent local counters.  Data advances for
  '  every changed version of the care; shape advances only when the
  '  care's live domain changes.  Shape implies data, but is not a
  '  position in the data timeline.
  :  data=nat shape=nat
+  yuga
  '  A node's versioning information: one lock per care, plus the
  '  apollo time and the PKI blockheight at mint.
  :  x=lock
     y=lock
     z=lock
     now=nat
     block=nat
+  oath
  '  Unsigned security scaffolding. Both fields are zero in this port.
  '  Neither authentication nor predecessor-hash semantics are implemented;
  '  this layout is not a network verification contract.
  :  sig=nat prev_hash=nat
+  aeon
  '  Versioning plus security: everything about a committed version
  '  except the record itself.
  :  =yuga =oath
+  saga
  '  The committed version of a node: the aeon and the record.
  '  /sov/step adjusts the yuga as it applies diffs, so historical
  '  case queries are floor lookups, not subtree scans.
  '  The record rides behind a pin: each committed myth is one
  '  content-addressed unit, so snapshotting the sovereign
  '  re-serializes spines, never stored records (global.plan's
  '  small-pins discipline).  Version-only re-mints (ass/next over
  '  the held record) share the old pin verbatim.
  :  =aeon myth=pin[myth]
+  note
  '  One diff: replace the record, merge into it, or retract the
  '  node.  Versioning is the namespace's job — a diff carries none.
  +  make
    :  =myth
  +  poke
    :  =myth
  +  cull
    :
  &  note/make
     note/poke
     note/cull
+  care
  '  Read restriction: the node only (.x), the node plus its frontier
  '  — the nearest record-bearing descendants, transparent paths passing
  '  through (.y) — or the whole subtree (.z).
  &  care/x
     care/y
     care/z

  +  x
    :

  +  y
    :

  +  z
    :

  +  seg
    '  The care's /h path segment.
    '  ?=  ((care/seg .z) ($ts "z"))
    \  c=care
    ^  iota
    ?  c
     > .x  'x
     > .y  'y
     > .z  'z
+  hunt
  '  A cared path: the (care, path) pair that names both a place and
  '  a reach — .x the node alone, .y the node plus its direct kids,
  '  .z the whole subtree.  A face's rendering claim is one, riding
  '  as DATA at ['hunt] on the face record itself (a pail slot, so
  '  it is explorer-visible and pokeable live): p is spelled
  '  relative to the face's own mount root ([] = the root itself),
  '  so the claim survives mounting anywhere and needs no rebase.
  :  c=care p=path
+  safe
  '  A version-pinned cared read: the target's PER-CARE local DATA
  '  case (not a sovereign epoch), the care, and the path.  A safe
  '  names an immutable answer — its /h spelling (safe/spell) never
  '  changes meaning once minted — so a record slot holding one is
  '  a pinned reference: a citation when left alone, a LIVE LINK
  '  when the record carries the fresh kook, which keeps every
  '  top-level safe slot current as its target changes.
  :  ver=nat =care =path

  +  spell
    '  The /h path a safe dereferences through:
    '  /h/<care>/<ver>/<len>/<path>.
    '  ?=  ((safe/spell (safe 3 .x ['a 'b])) [($ts "h") ($ts "x") ($u 3) ($u 2) ($ts "a") ($ts "b")])
    \  s=safe
    ^  path
    =  head=path  ['h (care/seg s.care) ($u s.ver) ($u s.path.len)]
    head.weld(s.path)

  +  of_hunt
    '  A safe over a hunt's (care, path) at a known case.
    \  ver=nat h=hunt
    ^  safe
    |  safe ver h.c h.p
' Structural typing *of* the namespace.  Node-level enforcement is
' LIVE: a record carrying its lash at ['sys 'lash] is judged by the
' commit gate (lain_poke/guard_diffs via lain_poke/fit_check) — a write whose
' final record breaks its own contract rejects the whole event,
' except a write that CHANGES the lash (adoption over legacy data
' is allowed; the watch app's standing queries find the survivors).
' Soma/yoke subtree patterns and the dep side (fief) remain
' vocabulary only for now.
'
+  res
  '  A resolution result.  .null is a tombstone answer; .unknown is
  '  the absence of any answer.  Never collapse the two: a shrug is
  '  not a tombstone.
  (@@ v)
  &  res/known[v]
     res/null
     res/unknown

  +  known
    :  value=v

  +  null
    :

  +  unknown
    :

  +  same
    '  Extensional equality of resolution states.  Unknown and
    '  tombstone remain distinct; known values compare deeply, a
    '  pinned record by its content.
    \  a=res[v] b=res[v]
    ^  bool
    |  equal a b

  +  run
    '  Map a function over a known value; null and unknown ride.
    (@ w)
    \  fun={\ v}w r=res[v]
    ^  res[w]
    ?  r
     > (./known x)  (./known (fun x))
     > .null        .null
     > .unknown     .unknown

+  sign
  '  Per-care change grade for one path: 0 unchanged, 1 data moved,
  '  2 data and shape moved (a creation or removal; shape implies
  '  data within one commit).
  :  x=nat y=nat z=nat


' A nominal reference is an exact x data moment, not a floating path.
+ definition_reference
  : path=path case=nat

  + brand
    \ reference=definition_reference
    ^ nat
    | brand_encode reference.path reference.case
  + parse
    \ brand=nat
    ^ maybe[definition_reference]
    ?> (./some decoded) (brand_decode brand) .none
    = [target version] decoded
    | ./some (definition_reference target version)
  + matches
    \ held=pail reference=definition_reference
    ^ bool
    | eq (nominal_brand held) reference.brand

